-- ============================================================================
-- PD3 EXPERT DEEP SEED: ESP Design, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE ELECTRICAL SYSTEM AND THE DIAGNOSIS. One number
-- carried through four translations, head per stage to head required to shaft
-- horsepower to amps at the surface, where an error introduced at any one of
-- them is invisible at the next.
--
-- THE TIER TEACHES AN ADJUDICATION, NOT A DEFECT LIST, and the reason is that
-- the two headline findings came out DIFFERENTLY.
--
--   TWO POWERS, RECORDED FOR A HUMAN DECISION. `shaftHp` is brake power at the
--   head REQUIRED; `stack.bhpTotal` is brake power at the head the stack
--   MAKES. The published motor sizing rule takes the second (PetroWiki, ESP
--   system selection and performance calculations) while this package builds
--   the amps, the drop and the cable pick on the FIRST, which always
--   understates. One quantity computed twice, so at most one can feed the
--   chain and the choice is open.
--
--   THE DERATE STOPPING AT THE MODULE SEAM, ADJUDICATED CORRECT. `sizePump`'s
--   `loadFraction` is utilisation against the motor's USABLE rating, because
--   the published selection rule divides required horsepower by the derating
--   factor. `motorCurrent`'s `loadFraction` is the ELECTRICAL load fraction
--   against the PLATE, because current at a given shaft load does not move
--   when permissible load is cut. Two different quantities sharing one name,
--   12.23 points apart on a real design. Both stand; the NAME is the defect.
--
-- The reader's test is one line: is this one thing computed twice, or two
-- things wearing one label.
--
-- THE CAPSTONE SITS ON THE CONSEQUENCE. On the capstone well OKARI-9 the
-- cable drop is 4.991671 percent against a 5 percent limit, which is eight
-- thousandths of a point of headroom. Take the OTHER power, the one the
-- published method names, and the amps go from 43.0628 to 43.321 A, the drop
-- goes to 5.0216 percent, the limit is crossed and the selected conductor
-- moves a full size from 1 AWG to 1/0. A tenth of a percent of horsepower buys
-- a cable size, which is why the choice cannot be waved through as noise.
--
-- A FAILS-OPEN, STATED HONESTLY. `selectCable`'s `ampacityOk` is TRUE BY
-- CONSTRUCTION, because the shipped `CABLE_SIZES` carry no ampacity column by
-- design, so `ok` collapses to `dropOk` alone and the published gate shows
-- 192 A taken down 6 AWG because the drop happens to pass. The honest
-- statement is that the check does not currently check anything, NOT that the
-- cable is wrong, and the difference between those two sentences is the
-- difference between a useful report and a false alarm.
--
-- AND THE ONE FIX OF FIVE THAT WAS MADE. `diagnoseOperation` formatted its
-- three ratio messages with no decimals, so a flag firing strictly below 85
-- percent printed "85 percent". One decimal place, no arithmetic changed, and
-- that is precisely why it was the one that could be made while the other four
-- could not: it moved a printed string rather than a number somebody's design
-- depends on. It NARROWS the collision by a factor of ten and does not remove
-- it, and the old format erred upward as readily as down.
-- ============================================================================

values ('esp', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-from-head-to-horsepower","title":"From Head to Horsepower","lesson_keys":["l01-what-shaft-power-is","l02-two-powers-for-one-pump","l03-which-one-the-method-takes","l04-what-the-difference-is-worth"]},{"key":"m02-the-motor","title":"The Motor","lesson_keys":["l01-nameplate-and-derate","l02-load-fraction","l03-the-derate-stops-at-the-seam","l04-one-name-two-quantities","l05-what-a-load-fraction-asserts"]},{"key":"m03-amps-and-cable","title":"Amps and Cable","lesson_keys":["l01-motor-current","l02-voltage-drop","l03-selecting-a-cable","l04-a-check-that-checks-nothing","l05-what-the-pick-runs-on"]},{"key":"m04-at-the-surface","title":"At the Surface","lesson_keys":["l01-surface-voltage","l02-kva","l03-cable-loss","l04-what-the-surface-numbers-are-for"]},{"key":"m05-diagnosis","title":"Diagnosis","lesson_keys":["l01-what-a-diagnosis-is","l02-the-three-ratio-flags","l03-a-warning-that-printed-its-own-threshold","l04-what-one-decimal-changed","l05-what-a-diagnosis-cannot-tell-you"]},{"key":"m06-the-expert-reading","title":"The Expert Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
